  "notes": "{弱|よわ}る means to weaken or to be troubled/at a loss.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Related transitive: {弱|よわ}める (to weaken something)\n\nTWO MAIN MEANINGS:\n1. Physical weakening: {体|からだ}が{弱|よわ}る (body weakens)\n2. Being troubled: {困|こま}って{弱|よわ}る (be troubled and at a loss)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {弱|よわ}っている: is weakened/troubled\n- {弱|よわ}った！: I'm in trouble! (interjection)\n- {弱|よわ}り{切|き}る: to be completely exhausted/at one's wits' end\n\nRELATED:\n- {弱|よわ}い: weak (adjective)\n- {弱|よわ}める: to weaken (transitive)\n- {弱|よわ}まる: to become weak (intransitive)\n\nNOTE:\n{弱|よわ}った used as an exclamation expresses being troubled or at a loss, similar to \"I'm stuck\" or \"What a problem!\"",
